      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T22:08:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of adding a new ApplicationExitInfo record, since the \"output\" should have included the records with native crashes, maybe we could just check if there is a record in the \u0027output\u0027 with REASON_CRASH_NATIVE, and its UID/PID matches with one of the records in the mTombstones, if yes, call `setNativeTombstonePfd` on that one",
      "revId": "8c3c7a9ba5537aba40b6413757e9a96f93c17a34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a71cec61_4cca5832",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/os/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 263,
      "author": {
        "id": 1079148
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T23:54:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there are 2 problems with this:\n\n1. the lifetimes of REASON_CRASH_NATIVE and the proto tombstone aren\u0027t the same: there\u0027s a window at the beginning of the crash where we\u0027ll have a REASON_CRASH_NATIVE, but no proto tombstone yet. If an app that forks a child and waits for it to return and then notices that it crashed, getHistoricalProcessExitReasons might give them a REASON_CRASH_NATIVE report without a proto tombstone, which will then gain one if it calls later. If other things crash, the proto tombstones can get deleted by other things crashing, which means the same REASON_CRASH_NATIVE can go from not having a proto tombstone to having one, back to not having one.\n\n2. there\u0027s a potential mismatch there: if the PID gets reused, we might attach the proto tombstone to the wrong crash (but that should be extremely rare). \n\nI think the most common use of apps using the proto tombstones is going to be an app searching only for proto tombstones to upload to their crash reporting, so it\u0027s probably better for us to separate them out more clearly?",
      "parentUuid": "a40b974e_0b1a36a3",
      "revId": "8c3c7a9ba5537aba40b6413757e9a96f93c17a34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
